# FT-1648: the explanation of each property row, the tooltip of its label: `field-help-<kind>-<path>`, else the
# member's `field-help-word-<member>` (see `strings::field_help`).
field-help-word-v = The version of this record's format in the file. It is kept for the file; you cannot change it.
field-help-word-id = The record's unique ID. It never changes, so links to the record keep working.
field-help-word-source-ref = Where the record came from when it was imported. An import uses it to find the record again; read only.
field-help-word-key = The record's key in the file it was imported from.
field-help-word-lineage = The import that brought the record into the project.
field-help-word-page = The page this is drawn on. Move it on the page or cut and paste it to change that.
field-help-word-colour = The wire colour as an IEC 60757 code (BK, BU, GNYE). A colour set here comes before the colour profile and the defaults.
field-help-word-csa = The cross-section of the wire in mm². A value set here comes before the size profile and the defaults.
field-help-word-insulation = The insulation type of the wire. A value set here comes before the project's default.
field-help-word-wire-part = The wire part from the library that the wire is made of; the wire list and the bill of materials name it.
field-help-word-function = The wire's function word, which the wire list prints. A value set here comes before the project's default.
field-help-word-shielded = Whether the wire is shielded. Ticked here, it is shielded whatever the levels below say.
field-help-word-twisted = Whether the wire is twisted in a pair. Ticked here, it is twisted whatever the levels below say.
field-help-word-flags = Whether the wire is shielded or twisted.
field-help-word-potential = The potential the wire or point lies on: the name its definition gives, else a name from the connections. Define potential… sets its name, type and voltage.
field-help-connection-kind = What kind of connection this is: a wire, a bridge or a fluid line.
field-help-connection-line-kind = What the fluid line carries: working, pilot, exhaust or drain, or a flexible hose. It sets how the line is drawn.
field-help-connection-number = The wire number as typed or frozen. Leave it empty to let wire numbering give it.
field-help-connection-derived-number = The wire number that is printed: from wire numbering, unless it is frozen. Freeze keeps it when the numbering changes.
field-help-connection-derived-colour = The colour the wire gets: its own override, else its cable core, its potential's definition, the colour profile or a default. The chip names the source; Go to source shows it.
field-help-connection-derived-csa = The cross-section the wire gets: its own override, else its cable core, its potential's definition, the size profile or a default. The chip names the source; Go to source shows it.
field-help-connection-derived-insulation = The insulation type the wire gets: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-wire-part = The wire part the wire gets: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-function = The function word the wire gets: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-shielded = Whether the wire is shielded: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-derived-twisted = Whether the wire is twisted: its own override, else its potential's definition or the project's default.
field-help-connection-overrides = The values set on this wire alone. Each comes before every other source of that value.
field-help-connection-overrides-colour = A colour for this wire alone. Clear it to give the wire the colour of its potential or profile again.
field-help-connection-overrides-csa = A cross-section for this wire alone. Clear it to give the wire that of its potential or profile again.
field-help-connection-overrides-length = A length for this wire, typed by hand, for the wire list. Clear it when the length is not known.
field-help-connection-overrides-show-marker = Whether the wire prints its marker on the page: its number, cross-section and colour beside the wire.
field-help-connection-a = Where the wire starts: a connection point of a device or a junction.
field-help-connection-b = Where the wire ends: a connection point of a device or a junction.
field-help-word-route = The corners of the wire's path on the page, as grid cells. Edit route on the page changes them.
field-help-potential-def-name = The potential's name (L1, 24VDC). Wires and points on the potential are known by it.
field-help-potential-def-ptype = The kind of signal the potential carries: a phase, neutral, PE, DC plus or minus, or a signal. The colour profile chooses the wire colour by it.
field-help-potential-def-voltage = The potential's voltage in volts. The colour and size profiles choose by it, and the checks read it.
field-help-potential-def-env = Whether the potential is AC or DC, its frequency and its earthing.
field-help-potential-def-env-ac-dc = Whether the potential is alternating (AC) or direct (DC) current.
field-help-potential-def-env-frequency = The frequency of an AC potential in hertz.
field-help-potential-def-env-earthing = How an extra-low voltage is earthed: PELV, SELV or floating.
field-help-potential-def-circuit-class = The circuit class of the potential: mains, control, analogue, bus or PE. The size profile chooses the cross-section by it; empty, it is derived.
field-help-potential-def-props = Wire properties for every wire on the potential. They come before the profiles and the defaults; a wire's own override comes before them.
field-help-potential-def-at = The point where the potential is defined: a connection point or a junction.
field-help-device-derived-tag = The device's tag as printed (-101K1): from its structure, letter and counter by the numbering scheme, unless it is frozen. Type another tag to freeze it.
field-help-device-tag = How the device's tag is made: its letter, its counter, a frozen tag and the numbering scheme.
field-help-device-tag-letter = The code letter of the tag (K for a contactor). Changing it renumbers the device.
field-help-device-tag-counter = The tag's number. Empty, numbering chooses the next free one.
field-help-device-tag-frozen = A tag kept as typed: numbering no longer changes it. Unfreeze to let numbering give the tag again.
field-help-device-tag-frozen-sign = Whether pages print the minus sign before the frozen tag.
field-help-device-tag-frozen-text = The frozen tag's text.
field-help-device-tag-scheme = The numbering scheme of this device; empty, the project's.
field-help-device-function-text = What the device does, in words (Main switch). Pages and reports print it beside the tag.
field-help-device-kind = What sort of device this is. It guides the tag letter and numbering.
field-help-device-state = Where the device is in its life: in use, a spare or planned.
field-help-device-parent = The device this one belongs to (an assembly, a manifold). Its tag follows the parent's.
field-help-device-position = The device's place inside its parent, such as a valve's place on a manifold.
field-help-device-process-tag = The process tag from the process drawing. Numbering never changes it.
field-help-device-parts = The parts the device is built from, each with its quantity. Choose part… adds one from the library.
field-help-device-parts-item-part = The part from the library, by its number and manufacturer.
field-help-device-parts-item-qty = How many of the part the device uses.
field-help-device-tech-data = Technical data of the device, each a name and a value (rated current, coil voltage).
field-help-device-tech-data-item-key = The name of the technical value.
field-help-device-tech-data-item-value = The technical value.
field-help-device-derived-cp-item = A connection point of the device, as pages print it. Mark not used tells the checks it stays free on purpose.
field-help-device-derived-main-location = Where the device's main symbol stands: its page and grid cell.
field-help-device-derived-printed-label = The text the device prints beside its tag.
field-help-device-derived-group = The group of the terminal on its strip. Typing a caption here names the group.
field-help-device-derived-structure-function = The function (=) identifier the tag uses: set on the device, else taken from its page or a structure box.
field-help-device-derived-structure-location = The location (+) identifier the tag uses: set on the device, else taken from its page or a structure box.
field-help-word-structure = The structure identifiers set here. One left empty is taken from the page or a structure box.
field-help-device-structure-function = The function (=) identifier of the device. Empty, the page's or a structure box's applies.
field-help-page-structure-function = The function (=) identifier of the page; the devices on it take it unless they set their own.
field-help-word-location = The location (+) identifier: where it is mounted. Devices without their own take the page's.
field-help-word-document-kind = The document kind (&) identifier of the structure.
field-help-word-functional-assignment = The functional assignment (==) identifier of the structure.
field-help-word-installation-site = The installation site (++) identifier: the plant or building.
field-help-word-type = The type (#) identifier of the structure.
field-help-word-user-defined = An identifier of your own kind, beside the standard ones.
field-help-device-strip = The terminal strip's own settings: how its terminals are named and printed.
field-help-device-strip-accessories = The strip's accessories (end brackets, covers) in mounting order.
field-help-device-strip-designation-scheme = How the terminals are numbered: 1, 2, 3 or another scheme.
field-help-device-strip-field-side = Which side of the terminals faces the field wiring.
field-help-word-groups = Groups of terminals on the strip, each with a caption.
field-help-device-strip-groups-item-from-seq = The first terminal of the group, by its place on the strip.
field-help-device-strip-groups-item-to-seq = The last terminal of the group, by its place on the strip.
field-help-device-strip-groups-item-label = The group's caption, printed above its terminals.
field-help-device-strip-label-mode = What the terminals print on the page: their designation or more.
field-help-device-strip-tag-print = Where the strip's tag is printed: once per segment or at every terminal.
field-help-device-terminal = This terminal's settings on its strip.
field-help-device-terminal-designation = The terminal's designation (1, 2, PE), printed at the terminal.
field-help-device-terminal-levels = The levels of a multi-level terminal, each with its own connection points.
field-help-device-terminal-rail-bonded = Whether the terminal is bonded to the mounting rail, as a PE terminal is.
field-help-device-terminal-seq = The terminal's place on its strip, for drawing and mounting; its designation may differ.
field-help-device-terminal-strip = The strip this terminal belongs to.
field-help-device-cable = The cable's own settings: its length and how its cores are named.
field-help-device-cable-core-id-mode = How the cable's cores are identified: by number or by colour.
field-help-device-cable-length = Where the cable's length comes from, or the length itself.
field-help-device-cable-pre-assembled = Whether the cable comes pre-assembled with its connectors.
field-help-device-plc-module = The PLC module's settings: its slot and its first addresses. A card gets them from its CPU, so it has none until a CPU is placed (the PLC panel lists a card under its CPU).
field-help-device-plc-module-integrated = Whether the module is built into the station's CPU.
field-help-device-plc-module-part-use = Which of the device's parts is the module.
field-help-device-plc-module-slot = The module's slot in the rack: auto for the next free one, or a number.
field-help-device-plc-module-start = The first input and output addresses of the module.
field-help-device-plc-module-start-input = The module's first input address: auto, or an address such as I4.0.
field-help-device-plc-module-start-output = The module's first output address: auto, or an address such as Q4.0.
field-help-device-plc-station = The PLC station's settings: its configuration project and its order.
field-help-device-plc-station-config-project = The PLC configuration project the station belongs to.
field-help-device-plc-station-order = The station's place among the stations of its configuration project.
field-help-device-plc-station-role = The station's role, such as the head station or a remote one.
field-help-device-assembly = The assembly's settings: what its bill of materials lists.
field-help-device-assembly-bom-basis = Whether the bill of materials lists the assembly's order codes or its components.
field-help-word-configs = The assembly's configured products, each an order code.
field-help-word-covers = The devices whose own part lines this order code replaces in the bill of materials.
field-help-device-assembly-configs-item-label = The configured product's label (Order code 1).
field-help-word-order-code = The order code, as the supplier writes it.
field-help-device-assembly-configs-item-part = The part of the configured product.
field-help-function-kind = What the function is: a normal function, an interruption point or a black box.
field-help-function-kind-ip = The interruption point's settings: its name, direction and order.
field-help-function-kind-ip-name = The name that pairs this interruption point with the others of the same name; the cross-reference shows where they are.
field-help-function-kind-ip-direction = Whether the signal leaves (source) or arrives (target) here, or goes both ways.
field-help-function-kind-ip-sort = The point's place in the chain of points with the same name.
field-help-function-kind-ip-star-source = Whether this point is the one the others of its name start from, in star mode.
field-help-function-kind-ip-external = The point outside the project this interruption point leads to.
field-help-function-role = Whether the function is the device's main function or an auxiliary one (a contact of a contactor).
field-help-function-def = The function definition this function was made from: its connection points and their names.
field-help-function-device = The device the function belongs to.
field-help-function-template-entry = Which function of the part this is, with its connection point names.
field-help-word-cp-overrides = Changes to single connection points of this function: another name, a description, or not used.
field-help-word-idx = Which connection point of the function this is, by its number in the function.
field-help-word-alias = A second name of the connection point, printed with its own (1 / L1).
field-help-function-cp-overrides-item-designation = The name the connection point prints instead of its definition's.
field-help-function-cp-overrides-item-description = A description of the connection point.
field-help-word-unused = Whether the connection point stays free on purpose; its unconnected-point finding is then only an info.
field-help-word-closure = How an unused fluid port is closed: a plug, a silencer or a blanking.
field-help-word-bus-port = The function's port on a field bus: its bus, address and net.
field-help-function-bus-port-address = The station address on the bus, or TBD while it is not known.
field-help-word-bus = The bus system (PROFINET, PROFIBUS).
field-help-word-interface = The interface name (DP, X1).
field-help-word-logical-net = The logical net of the port: where its address must be unique.
field-help-word-physical-net = The physical net whose cable segments the port belongs to.
field-help-word-port-label = The port's label on an interface with several ports (P1R).
field-help-function-bus-port-role = The port's role on the bus: master or device.
field-help-word-termination = The state of the port's termination switch.
field-help-representation-derived-xref = The cross-reference the symbol prints: where its other symbols or paired points are, by the project's format.
field-help-representation-pos = Where the symbol stands on the page, in millimetres and its grid cell. Move it on the page to change it.
field-help-representation-orient = How the symbol is turned and mirrored. Rotate and Mirror change it.
field-help-representation-symbol = The symbol from the library that draws this function.
field-help-representation-variant = The symbol's variant, such as another contact image.
field-help-representation-rep-type = Which view the symbol belongs to: multi-line, single-line or another.
field-help-word-functions = The functions this symbol draws.
field-help-representation-anchor = The point of the symbol that cross-references point to.
field-help-representation-arrangement = How the symbol's texts are arranged around it.
field-help-representation-pin-map = Which connection point of the symbol stands for which of the function.
field-help-representation-box = The outline and connection points of a black box.
field-help-word-cps = The connection points of the black box, each with its place and direction.
field-help-representation-box-cps-item-pos = Where the connection point lies on the box.
field-help-word-dir = The direction a wire leaves the connection point.
field-help-word-outline = The corners of the black box's outline.
field-help-representation-box-inner = Whether the box is drawn inside another symbol.
field-help-word-text-slots = The symbol's texts that are moved, turned or hidden here, each by its slot.
field-help-representation-text-slots-item-slot = Which text of the symbol this is (the tag, the function text).
field-help-representation-text-slots-item-pos = Where the text stands, from the symbol's origin.
field-help-word-angle = The angle the text is turned by.
field-help-word-visible = Whether the text is shown.
field-help-junction-at = Where the junction stands on the page.
field-help-word-sequence = The wires of the junction in wiring order; the first is the feed.
field-help-junction-style = How the junction is drawn: a dot or a bevel.
field-help-junction-wiring = Whether the wires are joined as a star or a chain; empty, the style's default.
field-help-page-item-kind = What the item is: a text, a graphic, an image, a wire marker or a view of a mounting surface.
field-help-page-item-kind-free-text = The text and how it is set.
field-help-page-item-kind-graphic = The shape and how it is drawn.
field-help-page-item-kind-image = The image and its size.
field-help-page-item-kind-wire-marker = The wire marker's settings.
field-help-page-item-kind-surface-view = The view of a mounting surface on a panel layout page.
field-help-word-surface = The mounting surface the page shows.
field-help-word-label-mode = What the placed devices print on the layout: their tag, part or nothing.
field-help-word-datum = The surface's point from which positions are measured.
field-help-word-datum-at = Where the measuring point of the surface lies on the page.
field-help-page-item-layer = The layer the item is drawn on.
field-help-page-title = The page's title, printed in its title block and in the table of contents.
field-help-page-folio = The page's folio: its number and section.
field-help-page-folio-number = The page's number within its section.
field-help-page-folio-section = The section the page belongs to.
field-help-page-folio-label = A folio label of your own, such as 101a.
field-help-page-kind = The page type: schematic, panel layout, report or another.
field-help-page-derived-description = The description the title block prints: the project's description, unless the page overrides it.
field-help-page-description-override = A description for this page alone, instead of the project's.
field-help-page-form = A frame of its own for this page, instead of the project's.
field-help-page-scale = The drawing scale of the page, such as 1:10.
field-help-page-grid = The page's connection grid: the step that symbols and wires snap to.
field-help-page-grid-num = The grid step's multiplier, in nanometres.
field-help-page-grid-den = The grid step's divisor.
field-help-section-title = The section's title.
field-help-section-number = The section's number.
field-help-section-divider = Whether the section starts with a divider page.
field-help-section-folio-range = The folios the section's pages use.
field-help-report-block-derived-kind = The page type of a generated page: report.
field-help-report-block-title = The title of the report's pages; a number is added per page.
field-help-report-block-source = What the report lists: devices, wires, terminals or parts.
field-help-report-block-form = The form the report's pages are laid out in.
field-help-report-block-continuation = The form of the report's further pages.
field-help-report-block-section = The section the report's pages go into.
field-help-report-block-first-folio = The folio of the report's first page.
field-help-report-block-sort = How the report's rows are sorted.
field-help-report-block-group = How the report's rows are grouped.
field-help-report-block-empty = Whether the report makes a page when it lists nothing.
field-help-report-block-embedded = Whether the report is printed inside another page.
field-help-report-block-manual = Rows added to or left out of the report by hand.
field-help-word-include = Records added to the report by hand.
field-help-word-exclude = Records left out of the report by hand.
field-help-project-kind = Whether this is a schematic project, a basic project or a macro project.
field-help-project-basic-project = The basic project this project was made from.
field-help-project-control-voltage = The project's control voltage.
field-help-project-derivation-profile = The version of the rules that derive tags, colours and sizes.
field-help-project-rated-consumption = The project's rated power consumption.
field-help-project-languages = The project's languages: the one texts are written in, and the translations.
field-help-project-master = The project's own data, which the title blocks print.
field-help-project-master-description = The project's description; every page prints it unless it overrides it.
field-help-project-master-document-title = The title of the document set.
field-help-project-master-long-description = A longer description of the project.
field-help-project-master-drawing-id = The drawing ID the title blocks print.
field-help-project-master-object-id = The ID of the object or machine the project is for.
field-help-project-master-project-ref = The project reference the title blocks print.
field-help-project-master-manufacturing-year = The year the equipment is built.
field-help-project-master-created = When the project was created.
field-help-project-master-edited = When the project was last edited.
field-help-word-parties = The people and companies of the project: customer, end user, panel builder, author.
field-help-project-parties-item-name = The party's name.
field-help-project-parties-item-role = The party's role in the project.
field-help-project-parties-item-address = The party's address.
field-help-word-street = The street and number.
field-help-word-postcode = The postcode.
field-help-word-city = The city.
field-help-word-country = The country.
field-help-project-parties-item-personal-data = Whether the party is a person whose data must be protected.
field-help-project-settings = The project's settings: numbering, profiles, formats and checks.
field-help-project-settings-colour-profile = The colour profile: which wire colour each kind of potential gets. Change it in the wizard.
field-help-project-settings-size-profile = The size profile: which cross-section each circuit class gets. Change it in the wizard.
field-help-project-settings-numbering = How device tags and wire numbers are made.
field-help-project-settings-xref-format = How cross-references are written, such as 102-A1.
field-help-project-settings-text-styles = The project's text styles: fonts and sizes.
field-help-project-settings-checks = Which checks run and how strict they are. The wizard's check step sets it.
field-help-project-settings-formatting = How dates and decimals are written, and whether tags are case sensitive.
field-help-project-settings-formatting-date = How dates are written.
field-help-project-settings-formatting-decimal-separator = Whether decimals use a point or a comma.
field-help-project-settings-formatting-tag-case = Whether tags that differ only in case are different tags.
field-help-project-settings-identifier-set = The set of code letters the tags use.
field-help-project-settings-ip-pairing = How interruption points of one name are paired: as a star or a chain.
field-help-project-settings-revision-label = How revisions are labelled: V1.0, 01 or A.
field-help-project-supply = The supply the equipment is connected to.
field-help-project-supply-u-nom = The supply's nominal voltage.
field-help-project-supply-frequency = The supply's frequency in hertz.
field-help-project-supply-phases = The number of phases of the supply.
field-help-project-supply-neutral = Whether the supply has a neutral.
field-help-project-supply-pe = Whether the supply has a protective earth.
field-help-project-supply-earthing = The supply's earthing system: TN-S, TN-C-S, TT or IT.
field-help-project-supply-origin = Where the supply comes from and how strong it is.
field-help-project-supply-origin-source = The device that feeds the equipment.
field-help-project-supply-origin-ik-max = The highest short-circuit current at the supply, in kA.
field-help-project-supply-origin-upstream-rating = The rating of the protection upstream of the supply, in A.
field-help-device-parts-item = One part the device uses, with its quantity.
field-help-device-tech-data-item = One technical value of the device: its name and value.
